TEXT -144 224 Left 2 ;The vntol parameter is rather high\n(to achieve fast simulation)
TEXT -336 176 Left 2 ;Delta Q is about 20MVAR\nat full load
TEXT -352 0 Left 2 ;If you plot Q you can see that the synchronous machine\nconsumes more and more Q if the P output gets higher \nand higher. This is although the voltage is regulated by\nAVR at 400kV. If the vsoll value is set to a higher value\nthe Q consumtion can be compensated by the higher\nmagnetic field voltage
TEXT -48 56 Left 2 ;You can set the \nvsoll parameter of \nthe pv-generator to 401.5kV\nlet the generator consume\nless Q at high load
TEXT -576 -24 Left 5 ;Comparison steady state PV element and transient PV element = synchronous generator with AVR
TEXT 128 32 Left 2 ;If the gradient of P is slow (endtime=150s instead of 15s) the max Q value is about 120MVar\nIf the gradient of P is medium is 1/2 (endtime=30s instead of 15s) the max Q (transient) )value is about 200MVar\nIf the gradient of P is fast  (endtime=15s) the max Q (transient) value is about 400MVar\nNote: The end (steady state) value of all three gradients is the SAME !!!!! (about 100MVAr)\nthey only differs for the increasing P time
